\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The hybrid TT. The grid is split into coarse blocks. The dense head stores, for every block $B$, the $\chi $ coefficients $A^0[B,\alpha ]$. The tail is a TT over the remaining bits (Morton order) and encodes $\chi $ fine-scale shape functions $\Phi _\alpha $ shared by all blocks. The large scales are therefore stored without rank error; only the fine structure is compressed.}}{2}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:encoding}{{1}{2}{The hybrid TT. The grid is split into coarse blocks. The dense head stores, for every block $B$, the $\chi $ coefficients $A^0[B,\alpha ]$. The tail is a TT over the remaining bits (Morton order) and encodes $\chi $ fine-scale shape functions $\Phi _\alpha $ shared by all blocks. The large scales are therefore stored without rank error; only the fine structure is compressed}{figure.1}{}}
