\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces One time step. Top (orange): the TT pipeline. Each right-hand-side evaluation is a chain of MPO--MPS products truncated to bond $\chi $. The Runge--Kutta stages are combined and truncated. The compressed result $\tilde  \theta _{n+1}$ is then projected onto the physical mass and variance, which are integrated alongside by the same stepper (green): a uniform field restores the mass and one scalar rescales the fluctuation. Bottom (grey): the dense twin, with identical inputs and the same projection but no truncation. A lossless TT run reproduces it to round-off.}}{4}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:step}{{3}{4}{One time step. Top (orange): the TT pipeline. Each right-hand-side evaluation is a chain of MPO--MPS products truncated to bond $\chi $. The Runge--Kutta stages are combined and truncated. The compressed result $\tilde \theta _{n+1}$ is then projected onto the physical mass and variance, which are integrated alongside by the same stepper (green): a uniform field restores the mass and one scalar rescales the fluctuation. Bottom (grey): the dense twin, with identical inputs and the same projection but no truncation. A lossless TT run reproduces it to round-off}{figure.3}{}}
