\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Renewal construction of the Kraichnan velocity. In each interval of length $\tau $ the velocity is one plane-wave mode with random wavevector and phase (blue stripes: lines of constant streamfunction; red: the velocity, along the stripes), held fixed while the scalar is advanced by ordinary sub-steps. Orange: the forcing kick at $k\approx 3$ added at the end of each interval. Each mode is the discrete curl of a plane-wave streamfunction, so it is exactly divergence-free on the grid and an exact rank-2 TT. As $\tau \to 0$ at fixed variance per unit time, the velocity becomes white in time.}}{7}{figure.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:kraichnan}{{4}{7}{Renewal construction of the Kraichnan velocity. In each interval of length $\tau $ the velocity is one plane-wave mode with random wavevector and phase (blue stripes: lines of constant streamfunction; red: the velocity, along the stripes), held fixed while the scalar is advanced by ordinary sub-steps. Orange: the forcing kick at $k\approx 3$ added at the end of each interval. Each mode is the discrete curl of a plane-wave streamfunction, so it is exactly divergence-free on the grid and an exact rank-2 TT. As $\tau \to 0$ at fixed variance per unit time, the velocity becomes white in time}{figure.4}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Dense Kraichnan runs against the exact lattice spectrum (white-noise limit). Top: $\xi =2$; bottom: $\xi =4/3$. Left: time-averaged spectra (symbols) and theory (lines). Centre: their ratio, for two Kubo numbers and two time steps. Right: variance histories, with the theoretical mean dashed.}}{7}{figure.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:kvalid}{{5}{7}{Dense Kraichnan runs against the exact lattice spectrum (white-noise limit). Top: $\xi =2$; bottom: $\xi =4/3$. Left: time-averaged spectra (symbols) and theory (lines). Centre: their ratio, for two Kubo numbers and two time steps. Right: variance histories, with the theoretical mean dashed}{figure.5}{}}
